# Named `Dockerfile.dockerignore`, NOT `.dockerignore`.
#
# Docker reads `<context>/.dockerignore`, and the context here is the repo root
# — so a `.dockerignore` sitting next to this Dockerfile is silently ignored.
# BuildKit's per-Dockerfile convention is `<dockerfile-name>.dockerignore`, and
# it is the only form that works for a Dockerfile outside its own context.
# Getting this wrong is not cosmetic: it put `services/render/.env`,
# secrets and all, straight into the image.
#
# Paths are relative to the REPO ROOT, since that is the build context.
#
# Without this the context is the whole monorepo including every app's
# node_modules and the mobile app's iOS build output — hundreds of megabytes
# uploaded to the daemon on every build, for files the image then discards.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.next
**/.next-dev
**/.turbo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# The other apps. The service imports `packages/*`, never these.
apps/mobile
apps/web
examples/studio
examples/demo
examples/demo-next
examples/webview-host

.git
.github
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log
**/.env
**/.env.*
